  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the City Winery in New York on April 19, 2016, following a previous archived show at the same venue on April 18 [2]. This recording is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones, capturing the full live atmosphere [1]. The setlist includes the only archived performances of “Rainbow in the Dark” and “Superman,” making these tracks particularly valuable for collectors [2]. Fans will also appreciate the appearance of “Cobscook Bay,” which had not been played in 32 previous archived shows [2]. The band shared stories about game shows and gimmicks between songs, adding a personal touch to the performance [1]. The show concludes with a lengthy encore, featuring the mythically rare “Home on the Range,” one of only two archived performances of that song [2]. This recording is the only available capture of this specific date, making it a valuable document of the band’s live work [1]. The visual materials for the event include a poster and fan art, both credited to Themes [3][4]. This performance is the 222nd in the archive’s collection for the band [2]. Listeners can expect a complete, well-documented experience of this particular night in New York [1].",
